      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For highly irregular, overtly structural textures like \"gnarled\" or \"bumpy\" that suggest significant surface abnormality, look toward codes describing dermatosis or skin reactions rather than purely pigmented lesions. Consider categories related to papillomatosis or other specific forms of skin dysplasia that denote gross textural changes. If the underlying pathology involves surface disruption, codes for bullous diseases or keratinization disorders might be more appropriate than morphology codes. Ultimately, documenting the underlying pathological process, like erosions or significant scaling, will help select the most precise non-pigmentary code.",
      "source": "target",
